# oracle: cut-down examples/body/in.pour3d: one rounded cube molecule (molecule.cube, 8 vertices, 12 edges, 6 faces, rounded diameter 0.5) poured with fix pour mol (seed 4767548, vol 0.4 10) into a slab above a fix wall/body/polyhedron floor, pair body/rounded/polyhedron 20 5 0 1 0.5 with pair_coeff * * 100 1, fix nve/body, fix gravity, 3000 steps: thermo atoms ke pe etotal press and the atom state
# Measured max relative error: 1.3e-11 (fx of atom 1; thermo 8.1e-14; positions 8.6e-15, velocities 4.1e-12). Native: installed lmp (LAMMPS 2 Sep 2026, BODY package). Native fixture: 3 bodies by step 500, 6 by step 2500 (the second fix pour event), pe nonzero from the floor contact (wall/body/polyhedron).
# oracle-inputs: w152body_pour_cube.mol
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all rel=1e-8 abs=1e-12
units           lj
dimension       3
boundary        p p fm
atom_style      body rounded/polyhedron 1 8
region          reg block 0 20 0 20 0 20 units box
create_box      1 reg
molecule        obj w152body_pour_cube.mol
pair_style      body/rounded/polyhedron 20 5 0 1 0.5
pair_coeff      * * 100 1
comm_modify     vel yes
neighbor        0.5 bin
neigh_modify    every 1 delay 0 check yes
timestep        0.001
fix             1 all nve/body
fix             2 all gravity 1.0 spherical 0.0 -180.0
region          slab block 5 15 5 15 3 6 units box
fix             ins all pour 8 0 4767548 vol 0.4 10 region slab mol obj
fix             4 all wall/body/polyhedron 2000 50 50 zplane 0.0 NULL
thermo_style    custom step atoms ke pe etotal press
thermo_modify   format float %.15g
thermo          500
run             3000
